helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	vi	A bitmap image can be inserted in $[officename] Writer, $[officename] Calc, $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	vi	Chọn lệnh \<emph\>Chèn > Ảnh > Từ tập tin\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149236				0	vi	Select the file. In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box you can restrict the selection to certain file types.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126				0	vi	Click the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box if you want a link to the original file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306				0	vi	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is marked, whenever the document is updated and loaded the bitmap image is reloaded. The editing steps that you have carried out in the local copy of the image in the document are re-applied and the image is displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336				0	vi	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is not marked, you are always working with the copy created when the graphic was first inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	vi	To embed graphics that were first inserted as links, go to \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Break Link\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	vi	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to insert the image.				20200411 15:09:53
