helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552				0	vi	When you select the bitmap image, the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar offers you the tools for editing the image. Only a local copy is edited in the document, even if you have inserted an image as a link.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	vi	The \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar may look slightly different depending to the module you are using.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124	13			0	vi	A number of filters are located on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/24010000.xhp\" name=\"Graphic Filter\"\>Graphic \<emph\>Filter\</emph\>\</link\> toolbar, which you can open with the icon on the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id7055574				0	vi	The original picture file will not be changed by the filters. Filters are applied to a picture only inside the document. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	vi	Some of the filters open a dialog, which you can use to select, for example, the intensity of the filter. Most filters can be applied multiple times to increase the filter effect.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	vi	In $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress, you can add text and graphics, select these objects together with the bitmap, and export the selection as a new bitmap image.				20200411 15:09:53
