helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	vi	If you want to exchange data with a database that does not have an ODBC link and does not allow dBASE import and export, you can use a common text format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145313				0	vi	Importing Data into $[officename]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	vi	To exchange data in a text format use the $[officename] Calc import/export filter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	vi	Export the desired data from the source database in a text format. The CSV text format is recommended. This format separates data fields by using delimiters such as commas or semi-colons, and separates records by inserting line breaks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	vi	Choose \<emph\>File - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>\<emph\>Open\</emph\>\</link\> and click the file to import.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id1977904				0	vi	Select "Text CSV" from the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> combo box. Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	vi	The \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Text Import\"\>\<emph\>Text Import\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears. Decide which data to include from the text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986				0	vi	Once the data is in a $[officename] Calc spreadsheet, you can edit it as needed. Save the data as a $[officename] data source:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	vi	Save the current $[officename] Calc spreadsheet in dBASE format in the folder of a dBASE database. To do this, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>, then select the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> "dBASE" and the folder of the dBASE database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150400				0	vi	Exporting in CSV Text Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140				0	vi	You can export the current $[officename] spreadsheet in a text format which can be read by many other applications.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	vi	Chọn \<emph\>Tập tin > Lưu dạng\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154216				0	vi	In \<emph\>File type\</emph\> select the filter "Text CSV". Enter a file name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	vi	This opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"dBase Export\"\>\<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, in which you can select the character set, field delimiter and text delimiter. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. A warning informs you that only the active sheet was saved.				20200411 15:09:53
